{"agent":"lk-probe","data":{"body":"LK-conflict-probe runs its old-git fallback through ci.merge_tree, which has no timeout parameter. The probe waits for it on a worker thread for probe_timeout_s and returns unavailable (never clean), but the worker keeps running to git's own GIT_TIMEOUT and the CLI process stays alive until it ends (critic findings 18 and 19, kimi-class reviewers). Fix: give services/ci/scratch.merge_tree and infra worktree scratch_tree a deadline that kills the git child and removes the worktree, then drop the thread in services/probe.py _scratch. LOW follow-ups from LK-conflict-probe reviews: none other open.","globs":["ddflow/services/ci/scratch.py","ddflow/services/probe.py","tests/test_conflict_probe.py"],"line":"","needs":[],"parent":"P-lock-lifecycle","tags":[],"title":"ci.merge_tree takes a deadline and cancels its git work, so the probe's old-git scratch fallback is bounded by [locks].probe_timeout_s"},"id":"e536d8c321bf6f6da0976817a","kind":"task.added","lamport":134760,"schema":1,"subject":"LK-probe-scratch-deadline","ts":"2026-11-04T11:41:35.621385Z"}
